# User-facing copy case (platform-wide, strict)

Crawllex UI copy must be **unified** across every module. Do not invent local casing exceptions.

## Title case — labels and chrome

Use **title case** (capitalize the first letter of each word) for short UI chrome:

- Button, label, heading, menu, and tab copy
- Sheet / dialog **titles** and section headings
- Empty-state **titles** and short status labels
- Form field labels and detail-sheet field labels (`DetailFieldRow`, project detail fields)

Examples:

- ✅ `Forgot Password`
- ✅ `Send Reset Link`
- ✅ `Lead Details`
- ✅ `Full Name`
- ✅ `Services Interested In`
- ❌ `Forgot password`
- ❌ `Send reset link`
- ❌ CSS `uppercase` turning labels into `DATE` / `EMAIL`

## Sentence case — descriptions, supporting copy, and toasts

Use **sentence case** for longer supporting text and for **toast / notify feedback**:

- Page/section **subtitles** and **descriptions** (including `SheetDescription` and `DetailSectionHeading` description)
- Helper text under headings, hero lead paragraphs, and bullet supporting lines
- Empty-state **bodies** and in-form success/body paragraphs (not button labels)
- Toast / `notify.*()` messages (and matching backend API `message` strings)

Examples:

- ✅ `Enter your account email and we'll send reset instructions if the address is registered.`
- ✅ `Contact details, message, and any extra fields from import.`
- ✅ `Account created. Check your email.`
- ✅ `You do not have permission to invite users.`
- ❌ `Account Created. Check Your Email.`
- ❌ `Core Profile Fields For This User.`
- ❌ `Permission Summary For This Role.`

**Sizing:** field labels use `type-caption`; values use `type-body`. Do not use `type-caption-xs` + `uppercase` for field labels. `type-overline` is for `StatusChip` only.

**Code:** toast/feedback messages go through `notify.*()` in `lib/frontend/feedback/notify.ts`, which applies `formatFeedbackText()` from `lib/frontend/feedback/format.ts`. Author toast strings in **sentence case** at the source (frontend locales and backend API messages).

Match an external API message verbatim when displaying it as-is.

Canonical rule: `AGENTS.md` → **User-Facing Copy Case**.
